# L2 — docs/plans/l2-upgrade.md. The full profile stays loaded; teaching is
# natural language; the sentences are real technical prose. Internal queries
# check that the correction reaches the KNOWLEDGE (the wrong reading's facts
# are withdrawn, the re-read sentence's facts are kept), not only the IR.
# !timeout 3: a correction re-reads the sentence inside the same turn.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test a word kept inside the phrase replaces the wrong fact with the right one]
!timeout 3
> A float switch controls the sump pump.
!query semantic_binding(binary(control), float_switch, object(sump))
> how did you read the noun phrase
<~ sump
> pump belongs to the noun phrase
<~ Learned: float switch controls sump pump.
!query semantic_binding(binary(control), float_switch, object(sump_pump))
!query! semantic_binding(binary(control), float_switch, object(sump))
!query controls(float_switch, sump_pump)
> how did you read the noun phrase
<~ sump pump
> What does a float switch control?
<~ Sump pump.

[test a rejected sentence becomes knowledge after the correction]
!reset
!timeout 3
> Heat treatment relieves residual stress.
<~ I didn't keep that
> heat belongs to the noun phrase
<~ Learned: heat treatment relieve residual stress.
!query relieve(heat_treatment, residual_stress)
> What relieves residual stress?
<~ heat treatment

[test a false fact is withdrawn even when the re-read keeps nothing]
!reset
!timeout 3
> Expansive clay swells when it absorbs water.
!query semantic_binding(binary(absorb), expansive_clay_swells, object(water))
> how did you read the noun phrase
<~ expansive clay swells
> end the previous noun phrase before swells
<~ I have withdrawn what my first reading had kept
<! Learned
!query! semantic_binding(binary(absorb), expansive_clay_swells, object(water))
> how did you read the noun phrase
<~ expansive clay
<! swells

[test a word lesson transfers to sentences never corrected, and withdraws]
!reset
!timeout 3
> A float switch controls the sump pump.
> pump belongs to the noun phrase
> use that reading for pump in future sentences
<~ In future sentences I will read «pump» as part of a noun phrase.
!query reading_continuer_lesson(pump, $Example)
> The condensate pump returns water to the boiler.
> how did you read the noun phrase
<~ condensate pump
> A vacuum pump removes air from the condenser.
> how did you read the noun phrase
<~ vacuum pump
> forget that pump belongs to noun phrases
< I have withdrawn the lesson that «pump» belongs to noun phrases.
> The condensate pump returns water to the boiler.
> how did you read the noun phrase
<! condensate pump

[test an ending lesson transfers across an open class]
!reset
!timeout 3
# These memberships are prerequisite lessons, not L2 transfer successes.
> opens is a verb
> vents is a verb
# no pronoun here: the antecedent is stage 3 (its own test)
> A relief valve opens above the set pressure.
> end the previous noun phrase before opens
<~ I now end that noun phrase before «opens»
> which classes could share the boundary for opens
<~ verb
> use that reading for every verb
<~ I will read members of «verb» as the end of a noun phrase
!query reading_boundary_class(verb, $Example)
> A safety valve vents under pressure.
!query input_entity_node(current_turn, en, $Id, safety_valve)
!query! input_entity_node(current_turn, en, $Id, safety_valve_vents)
> unseats is a verb
> A pilot valve unseats under pressure.
!query input_entity_node(current_turn, en, $Id, pilot_valve)
> forget that unseats is a verb
> A pilot valve unseats under pressure.
!query input_entity_node(current_turn, en, $Id, pilot_valve_unseats)
> forget the boundary for every verb
< I have withdrawn the reading lesson for the class «verb».
> A safety valve vents under pressure.
!query input_entity_node(current_turn, en, $Id, safety_valve_vents)

[test a local correction is undone and never becomes a lesson]
!reset
!timeout 3
> A float switch controls the sump pump.
> pump belongs to the noun phrase
> undo the local boundary correction for pump
<~ I have withdrawn the local correction for «pump»
!query! reading_local_continuer($Quoted, pump)
!query! reading_revision($Scope, $Id, $Revision)
> The condensate pump returns water to the boiler.
> how did you read the noun phrase
<! condensate pump

[test ambiguous and absent occurrences cannot change a reading]
!reset
!timeout 3
> A relief valve opens opens under pressure.
> end the previous noun phrase before opens
<~ I cannot identify one uncorrected noun phrase
!query! reading_revision($Scope, $Id, $Revision)
> use that boundary for opens in future sentences
<~ I need one unambiguous corrected reading
!query! reading_boundary_lesson(opens, $Example)
> A relief valve opens under pressure.
> absentword belongs to the noun phrase
<~ I cannot find one uncorrected noun phrase
!query! reading_revision($Scope, $Id, $Revision)

[test the correction surface is knowledge: ablate it, add another, no rebuild]
!reset
!timeout 3
!forget turn_form(reading_phrase_extend, 2, text("belongs to the noun phrase"))
> A float switch controls the sump pump.
> pump belongs to the noun phrase
<! Learned: float switch controls sump pump.
!query! reading_local_continuer($Quoted, pump)
!assert turn_form(reading_phrase_extend, 2, text("is part of the noun phrase"))
> A float switch controls the sump pump.
> pump is part of the noun phrase
<~ Learned: float switch controls sump pump.
!query reading_local_continuer($Quoted, pump)

[test stage 3: the antecedent chosen by the text rewrite has a receipt and is corrected]
!reset
!timeout 3
# Only the receipt, the inspection and the correction are certified here: the
# sentence still does not become a fact (the reader takes «set» as its verb).
> opens is a verb
> A relief valve opens above its set pressure.
> what did its refer to
<~ I read «its» as «opens»
!query reading_choice($Scope, its, antecedent, choice(opens, most_recent))
> its refers to the relief valve
> what did its refer to
<~ I read «its» as «relief valve»
!query reading_local_antecedent($Quoted, its, relief_valve)
